ompared to the standard glass now along  with that this is apple's first desktop  display or display in a macbook that  actually runs at 600 nits the pro  display xdr for standard non-hdr content  runs at 500 as does this new 60-inch  macbook pro the 14-inch macbook pros the  imacs all those so that extra of 100  nits is also going to combat any  reflectivity now the next choice that  you get is the stand for an extra 400  you can upgrade to a hinged display that  allows for adjustment in height now that  stand that is similar looking to this  with the pro display xdr that i have is  a thousand bucks but what you have to  make sure that you don't miss is that  this does not allow for rotation or  removal or anything like that so that  price is just for height adjustment and  if you look at this image the display is  much closer to you if you have it kind  of in that normal range compared to  being tucked further back and that is  something that can be a pain with a lot  of desks over 400 bucks i don't think  it's worth it you can always get one of  those little stands to lift it up or  maybe even put it on your mac studio if  it fits on there moving on to the mac  studio we are greeted with a couple  options right out of the gate and one  thing that you guys have to know is that  it doesn't matter which one you choose  other than the base storage so this 4  000 option literally twice as expensive  we've never seen such a big jump it  right away doubles your ram and your ssd  so if you're somebody that doesn't need  a terabyte of ssd let's say you use a  server then you can go with the base  model and then upgrade the components  that you need now with that said with  this mac this is one of the few times  where i would suggest for people to  spend more money on storage in the past  i always said hey buy an external ssd or  hard drive don't waste too much money on  storage here but this time because apple  is using the fastest ssds on the market  and their prices are